{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nEvery COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar is emitted with `material=None` — `completion_sidecar.emit(result, material=None, repo_root=repo_root)` at `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:405`, with the comment at `:754` noting no fingerprint is computed on this path. Measured on the live store: 0 of the most recent 300 COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecars (216 PASS / 59 FAIL / 23 no-verdict / 2 ERROR) carry any material/material_fingerprint field.\n\n## Consequence (why this is worth fixing)\n\nA FAIL followed by a PASS on the same `verified_at_sha` cannot be attributed: verifier inputs include ticket comments and prefetched evidence, which change without a code commit, so \"no commit in between\" does not mean \"same inputs.\" This makes the completion gate's precision unmeasurable from its own records (an analysis this week mis-derived an \"80–84% FP\" figure from exactly this gap), and it means completion attestations cannot support the stale-material currency discipline that plan-review attestations already have.\n\nNote: the `material=None` is deliberate per the code's own comment — this ticket treats the capability gap as the defect (operator-directed filing, 2026-08-31). Formula/prompt version stamping in the same record would make longitudinal gate analysis version-aware (pass-3 blocking formulas have changed over time, so unversioned sidecars conflate formula eras).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecars (PASS, FAIL, ERROR alike) record a material fingerprint over the verifier's actual inputs (ticket material as pinned for the run: description/ACs/comments snapshot + evidence set identifiers), reusing the existing plan-review fingerprint machinery where applicable rather than inventing a new scheme.\n- [ ] Sidecars record the verifier formula/prompt version identifier alongside the fingerprint.\n- [ ] Existing sidecars are untouched (no backfill); consumers treat absent material as \"unknown era\".\n- [ ] A regression test asserts a FAIL sidecar carries a non-null fingerprint and version.\n\n## File impact\n\nTo be confirmed at investigation (bugs do not pre-declare impact): expected `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`, `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py` (or equivalent emitter), one test module.\n\n## Fix plan (2026-08-31)\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe completion verifier already computes/pins material identity (`material_fingerprint` plus the pinned `completion_read_basis` receipt) before close publication, but both close-time and standalone sidecar emitters pass `material=None`, and `completion_sidecar.build_payload` only serializes that explicit argument. The sidecar therefore drops the verifier-input identity it already has. The same COMPLETION_VERDICT event family also carries `gate_error_v1` ERROR records without a completion-verifier prompt/formula version.\n\n### Scope / file impact\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py`: make COMPLETION_VERDICT PASS/FAIL payload construction derive a non-null material fingerprint from the verifier result when the caller does not supply one, incorporating the existing plan-review material fingerprint and the pinned completion read-basis receipt digest when available; stamp the completion-verifier prompt version/content hash.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`: stop documenting the close-path sidecar as deliberately material-less and let the shared emitter enrich PASS/FAIL records without changing close outcomes.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py`: keep standalone `verify-completion` recording behavior/outcomes unchanged while allowing the shared emitter to enrich PASS/FAIL records.\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_error_sidecar.py`: for completion-gate ERROR sidecars, best-effort stamp the same material/version observability fields; preserve best-effort/no-outcome-change semantics.\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py`: RED→GREEN regression coverage that a FAIL sidecar carries non-null fingerprint and version, plus payload coverage for PASS/FAIL/ERROR era handling.\n\n### Acceptance criteria mapping\n\n- AC1: New PASS/FAIL sidecars will write `material_fingerprint` from existing verifier material (`result['material_fingerprint']`) and, when present, the pinned `completion_read_basis` receipt digest that represents the ticket/comments snapshot actually consulted. ERROR sidecars in the completion gate will best-effort compute current material identity so ERROR intervals are not unversioned/unknown when the verifier fails before a normal verdict.\n- AC2: New sidecars will carry `verifier_prompt_version` (completion-verifier prompt id + git-canonical content sha256) beside the fingerprint.\n- AC3: No migration/backfill/prune path is touched. Readers remain tolerant of absent material/version fields, so old sidecars stay \"unknown era\".\n- AC4: A regression test will assert a FAIL sidecar emitted through the public `completion_sidecar.emit` path carries non-null fingerprint and prompt version; it will be observed RED before production code changes and GREEN after.\n\n### Safety invariants\n\nThis is record enrichment only. It must not alter the completion PASS/FAIL/ERROR verdict, close blocking, signing eligibility, or whether sidecar persistence failures are swallowed. If any candidate change affects those gate outcomes, stop and seek an operator decision.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788233898909023001,"uuid":"97d1801a-d1dc-477f-953d-13d76bc4784c"}